    <string name="privacy_policy_body">Geo Tag Photo needs Camera and Location permissions to create geotagged photos.\n\nCaptured photos, recent-history references, selected date and time, and location details are processed on your device and saved to storage you control. This app does not require an account and does not include advertising or analytics SDKs.\n\nAndroid and Google Play location services may provide the device location. The system geocoder may turn coordinates into a place or address. The Choose on map screen loads OpenStreetMap tiles over the internet. When Map preview is enabled and a Google Maps API key is configured, coordinates are sent to the Google Maps Static API to create the map image. Those services handle requests under their own privacy policies.\n\nYou can edit or clear place, address, coordinates, date, and time before capture. You can revoke permissions at any time in Android Settings; features that require those permissions will stop working.\n\nThis policy describes the current app build and may be updated when its features change.</string>
    <string name="terms_of_use_body">Use Geo Tag Photo only where you have permission to capture, store, and share images. You are responsible for following local laws and respecting other people and private property.\n\nLocation, address, date, and time can be detected automatically or edited manually. Accuracy is not guaranteed, and edited metadata must not be treated as independent proof of where or when a photo was taken.\n\nThe app is provided as is, without warranties. You are responsible for reviewing photos and metadata before relying on or sharing them. Third-party location, geocoding, and mapping services are subject to their own terms.\n\nBy using the app, you agree to these terms.</string>
